["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/duns", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Data Universal Numbering System (D-U-N-S) Number](https://www.dnb.com/en-us/smb/duns.html) is a unique nine-digit identifier, issued by Dun & Bradstreet, that identifies a business entity, often on a location-specific basis.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/AssemblyAction", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "AssemblyAction represents the event of creating a product by assembling individual components.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N2407776fdcf64c43b6a058458273d996", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "_:Nd1322feff93e416188fa0b582bbb9ad5", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isbn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Book Number (ISBN)](https://www.isbn-international.org/content/isbn-users-manual/29) is a unique numeric identifier for monographic publications standardized by [ISO 2108](https://www.iso.org/standard/65483.html). It consists of either 10 digits (for assignments prior to January 1, 2007) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISBN is composed of five parts: a GS1 prefix, a registration group, a registrant, a publication element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9780198836063`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/startTime", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp", "globalId", "", ""]
